:"https://api.github.com/users/Mikeysax","html_url":"https://github.com/Mikeysax","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mikeysax/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mikeysax/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mikeysax/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mikeysax/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mikeysax/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mikeysax/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mikeysax/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mikeysax/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mikeysax/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-23T15:28:19Z","updated_at":"2025-01-23T15:28:19Z","body":"> I can't reproduce this, assuming it's very intermittent, so would need some further ways to narrow down triggering this\n\nYeah, it's difficult to reproduce for me as I'm not sure when it occurs. It happens to me after many runs and code modification in either the child class or unrelated files","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2610116522/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2613968996","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101914#issuecomment-2613968996","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101914","id":2613968996,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6bzgBk","user":{"login":"Mikeysax","id":15805689,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1ODA1Njg5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15805689?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mikeysax","html_url":"https://github.com/Mikeysax","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mikeysax/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mikeysax/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mikeysax/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mikeysax/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mikeysax/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mikeysax/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mikeysax/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mikeysax/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mikeysax/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-25T13:37:54Z","updated_at":"2025-01-25T14:00:42Z","body":"I was able to trigger it again just now in my own project: \n\n- I had the parent and child script classes open in the script editor.\n- I closed the child script class files.\n- I modified the parent class code.\n- I ran the game.\n- The error triggered.\n\nIt seems it is triggered when modifying the parent class, the game/engine/language server, or something doesn't recognize the change needs to trickle down to it's children and ends up not compiling correctly and thus the function doesn't exist?\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c4f1fde2-fbfc-4281-a68d-e1ddd6711ac9)\n\nI was able to replicate this a couple times; I think the key is modifying the parent class code.\n\nHere is a video of it:\n\nhttps://youtu.be/YZfJzsDXZJU?si=eRMQcPKDSceepxE9\n\nIn the video, you can see:\n\n- I open the project\n- I show you which files I have open, one of which is the `InputComponent` which is the parent class of two other classes\n- I start the game and it runs fine\n- I stop running the game\n- I edit the parent class `InputComponent` and save it\n- I run the game again\n- The exception is then thrown","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2613968996/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2617383115","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101914#issuecomment-2617383115","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101914","id":2617383115,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6cAhjL","user":{"login":"Mikeysax","id":15805689,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1ODA1Njg5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15805689?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mikeysax","html_url":"https://github.com/Mikeysax","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mikeysax/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mikeysax/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mikeysax/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mikeysax/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mikeysax/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mikeysax/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mikeysax/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mikeysax/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mikeysax/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-28T01:10:14Z","updated_at":"2025-01-28T01:14:31Z","body":"Just an FYI, I've modified the code so that only the following is calculated in the Parent class and the `move_direction` code is called via a global utility class instead:\n\n# Defined in InputComponent\n```\nfunc _update_relative_y_axis() -> void:\n\tif _camera_component is CameraComponent:\n\t\trelative_y_axis = _camera_component.rotation.y\n\telse:\n\t\trelative_y_axis = _owner.rotation.y\n```\n\nThis results in the `else` value only being called even when the `_camera_component` is defined as verified via a `print` statement; The `relative_y_axis` ends up being `0.0`. \n\nThis method is now defined in the parent class:\n\n# In InputComponent, but reference via child PlayerInputComponent or NpcStateInputComponent\n```\nfunc move_direction() -> Vector3:\n\tif not is_input_direction_set: return Vector3.ZERO\n\treturn Util.get_move_direction(input_direction, relative_y_axis)\n```\n\nThen, this function is called via it's child class in a another class state:\n\n# In MoveState\n```\nfunc update_input_move_direction() -> void:\n\tinput_move_direction = _input_component.move_direction()\n```\n\nI think there is something odd going on in GDScript with inheritance, specifically when the Parent class is modified and child classes are referenced. It's like the child class doesn't know the parent changed.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2617383115/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2686279177","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101914#issuecomment-2686279177","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101914","id":2686279177,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6gHV4J","user":{"login":"cwchunwei","id":14936223,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0OTM2MjIz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14936223?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwchunwei","html_url":"https://github.com/cwchunwei","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwchunwei/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwchunwei/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwchunwei/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwchunwei/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cwchunwei/